Any idea why NuGet package Update-Package -Id Microsoft.Pex.VisualStudio does not work?
I'm using Visual Studio 2015 Enterprise and I have the latest updates installed, including NuGet packages. I also have the latest version of Pex installed.

A: According to the Microsoft documentation, updating NuGet package Microsoft.Pex.VisualStudio only available for Pex versions 2.0 and onwards. 
The error message suggests that you are using Pex 1.0, where the corresponding NuGet package for updating isn't available.
Upgrading to the newer Pex version should resolve this issue by updating the NuGet package Microsoft.Pex.VisualStudio.
For Pex 1.0, you'd use NuGet package Microsoft.Pex.VisualStudio 1.0. However, note that Pex 1.0 is not recommended for use with modern Visual Studio versions and may not work with them at all. Unless you specifically have this version installed, I'd recommend upgrading to a newer version of Pex.
